[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m. It uses the browser's own [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m, so clicking toggles it on and off
  with no JavaScript:

  [90m<[34mmain[90m>[39m
    [90m<[34mlabel[90m>[39m
      [90m<[34minput[90m [36mtype[90m=[31m"checkbox"[90m [36mid[90m=[31m"task-done"[90m>[39m
      Done
    [90m</[34mlabel[90m>[39m
  [90m</[34mmain[90m>[39m

  The checkbox sits inside a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, so clicking the "Done" text toggles it too, and screen readers announce it as
  "Done".

  The state isn't saved, so it resets when the page reloads. There aren't any task items on the page yet either, so this
  is a single checkbox. If you want one checkbox per task, or want the checked state to persist (for example with
  [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m), I can add that.

